# EtPost Component

Social post component following etoro-ui standards with compound component pattern.

## Overview

`EtPost` is the unified social post compound component; it follows modern etoro-ui architecture:

- **Compound Component Pattern** - Flexible composition with `EtPost.Header`, `.Body`, `.Image`, `.Video`, `.Link`, `.Trade`, `.Poll`, `.SharedPost` (with `.Header / .Body / .Attachment / .Deleted`), `.Footer`, `.Likes`, `.Comments`, `.Shares`, `.Save`
- **Compound Footer** - Engagement actions are flat subcomponents (`EtPost.Likes`, `.Comments`, `.Shares`, `.Save`) composed inside `EtPost.Footer`. Engagement data is NOT passed as props to `EtPost` itself.
- **Flat Attachment API** - Attachment sub-components are direct children of `EtPost` (no wrapper needed)
- **Context-Based State Sharing** - Minimal context (`haptics` only), subcomponents use `usePostContext()`
- **Delegated Text Expansion** - Body uses `EtReadMoreText` for expand/collapse (no manual state in context)
- **Memoized Performance** - `React.memo`, `useMemo`, `useCallback` throughout
- **Accessibility** - Full support for `testID`, `accessibilityLabel`, `accessibilityHint`

## Usage

### Basic Usage

```tsx
import { EtPost } from '@etoro-ui';

<EtPost
  displayName="Akansha Trivedi"
  avatar="https://example.com/avatar.jpg"
  location="Germany"
  text="This is something that annoys me..."
  timestamp="2h"
>
  <EtPost.Header />
  <EtPost.Body />
  <EtPost.Footer>
    <EtPost.Likes onPress={handleLike} isActive={isLiked}>{10}</EtPost.Likes>
    <EtPost.Comments onPress={handleComment}>{121}</EtPost.Comments>
    <EtPost.Shares>{33}</EtPost.Shares>
    <EtPost.Save onPress={handleSave} isActive={isSaved} />
  </EtPost.Footer>
</EtPost>;
```

